   "id": "hook",
   "text": "The US is reportedly weighing its biggest non-nuclear bomb for Iran. Why now?"
  },
  {
   "id": "f1",
   "text": "CNN reports the US military has drafted new strike options for Iran. Sources say they include the so-called mother of all bombs, aimed at energy infrastructure and nuclear sites. They would apply only if Trump orders combat to resume."
  },
  {
   "id": "f2",
   "text": "Several sources doubt it could reach the deepest targets, like Pickaxe Mountain. One called it a weapon for huge area clearance, but not much else. Trump told Newsmax the bomb is not nuclear, and he would not use nuclear weapons."
  },
  {
   "id": "f3",
   "text": "Trump has said publicly he will take no new action before the midterms. CNN says advisers privately don't know if that is final. Times of Israel reports Iran's parliament speaker says Tehran must prepare for war, even while negotiating."
  },
  {
   "id": "cta",
   "text": "Will the US strike Iran again before the midterms? Yes or no?"
  }
 ],
